It makes sense that, since we have input and output, we should make a diagram! Here's a diagram that connects everything that's in the problem with what we're after, $|z-w|$. [asy]
unitsize(0.15 cm);

pair A, B, C, D, O, P, Q;

O = (0,0);
A = -1 - 3*I;
B = 7 + 8*I;
C = -4 - I;
D = 4 + 2*I;

draw(Circle(A,1), red);
draw(Circle(B,3), blue);
draw(A--B);

dot("$z$", A, SE);
dot("$w$", B, SW);
dot("$-1-3i$", A, SE);
dot("$7+8i$", B, SW);
dot("$-4-i$", C, SE);
dot("$4+2i$", D, NW);
[/asy]With the circles drawn this way, $|z-w|$ is at least the distance between the farthest point on one circle and the nearest point on the other. So we want the distance between the centers of the circles minus the radius of the larger circle and the radius of the smaller circle. In other words, $|-1 - 3i - (7 + 8i)| - 1 - 3 = |-8 - 11i| - 1 - 3 = \sqrt{8^2 + (-11)^2} - 4 = \sqrt{233} - 4.$</think> <answer> $\sqrt{233} - 4$ </answer>

